; Component-level tests. Two parts, because each side is good at a different thing:
;
;   rt_test.ml  OCaml: builds each component in isolation and materialises it with
;               Vdom.Node.to_dom, and (the part that must be OCaml) drives real
;               events into the Bonsai graph with Bonsai_web_test's Handle.
;   run.mjs     node: sets up jsdom, runs the bundle, then asserts on the resulting
;               DOM — where the API is plain and already proven.
;
; Not inline_tests: those need dune's js backend, which looks for a library named
; "js" that does not exist in this switch. And a native link is impossible because
; virtual_dom pulls in js_of_ocaml's runtime (Ojs).
(executable
 (name rt_test)
 (modes js)
 (libraries astryx bonsai bonsai_web bonsai_web_test)
 (preprocess
  (pps bonsai.ppx_bonsai js_of_ocaml-ppx)))
